{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Switching an alerted provider to unlimited can leave an obsolete exhausted alert visible indefinitely, although routing remains correct."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"compat","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Exporting the configuration adds quota fields that the previous release rejects if the operator rolls back."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The MCP tool omits the quota mode for an unlimited provider, making its empty windows harder to interpret."}]}